.TH LIBRDP-TRACING 7 "2026-07-12" "librdp 0.1.0" "Miscellaneous Information Manual"
.SH NAME
librdp-tracing \- runtime trace controls for librdp
.SH DESCRIPTION
librdp trace is disabled by default and writes structured key-value lines to standard error. It is intended for interoperability, performance, parser, transport, graphics, input, channel, and backend diagnostics.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_CLIENT
Enable client lifecycle, viewer, framebuffer, input, pointer, clipboard, channel, audio, video, and backend events.
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_TRANSPORT
Enable TCP, TLS, UDP, read, write, wait, timeout, EOF, and close events.
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_PROTOCOL
Enable handshake, parser, PDU, capability, slow-path, fast-path, security, channel, and codec events.
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_LEVEL
Set verbosity. Accepted names are error, warn, info, debug, and trace. Numeric values 0 through 4 are also accepted.
.TP
.B LIBRDP_TRACE_HEX_BYTES
Maximum number of bytes emitted by bounded protocol hexdumps. Invalid or unset values use zero.
.SH FORMAT
Normal events use:
.P
.nf
librdp trace seq=<n> ts_ns=<n> elapsed_us=<n> category=<category> event=<name> level=<level> message="<fields>"
.fi
.P
Protocol hexdumps use:
.P
.nf
librdp trace seq=<n> ts_ns=<n> elapsed_us=<n> category=protocol event=<name> level=trace payload_len=<n> dumped=<n> hex=<bytes> ascii="<ascii>"
.fi
.SH SECURITY
Trace must not print passwords, authentication tokens, private keys, WebAuthn secrets, smartcard PIN-like data, clipboard contents, file contents, audio samples, or video frames. Prefer identifiers, sizes, result codes, flags, and timing data.
.SH DIAGNOSTIC USE
Use client trace for lifecycle, surfaces, input, pointer, clipboard, channel, audio, video, and backend behavior.
.P
Use transport trace for TCP, TLS, UDP, timeout, read, write, EOF, and close behavior.
.P
Use protocol trace for handshake, parser, PDU, capability, channel, fast-path, slow-path, security, and codec behavior.
.P
Enable bounded protocol hexdumps only when packet bytes are required for parser or interoperability analysis.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
LIBRDP_TRACE_CLIENT=1 LIBRDP_TRACE_PROTOCOL=1 librdp-viewer --target host --security nla

LIBRDP_TRACE_CLIENT=1 LIBRDP_TRACE_TRANSPORT=1 LIBRDP_TRACE_PROTOCOL=1 LIBRDP_TRACE_LEVEL=trace LIBRDP_TRACE_HEX_BYTES=96 librdp-viewer --target host --security nla
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR librdp (7),
.BR librdp-api (7),
.BR librdp-viewer (1)
